  "interpretation": {
    "declared_route_omission_established": true,
    "exact_source_finding": "The consumed worker selected the V6 context and V6 initial application, but its sole production advance call was advance_behavior_v4. That function passes use_r126_development_progression=false. No production call to advance_behavior_v5 existed in the invocation blob.",
    "first_decisive_step": "At candidate semantic step 59 the immutable classification satisfied raised_body, joint limits, actuator budget, exactly zero forbidden-contact impulse, and no-cheat while legacy energy safety remained false. The qualified R126 route would therefore have handed control to stance_handoff on this already-observed input; the invoked V4 route remained in raise_body.",
    "later_trajectory_limit": "The retained physical trajectory after step 59 belongs to the invoked legacy progression route. It cannot establish what the declared R126 progression route would have done after ownership changed, and no later trajectory is predicted here.",
    "preserved_partial_evidence": "World construction, 905 native solver steps, engine health, all in-run invariants, application-mutation semantics, native target writes, contacts, and body-raise observations remain exact partial evidence about what physically ran.",
    "invalid_behavior_inference": "Because the portable progression route named by the contract did not run, the accepted evaluator negative does not answer the declared R129 behavior question. Current live authority classifies the attempt as consumed infrastructure-invalid/incomplete for behavior inference.",
    "original_closure_preserved": "The R129 raw result and published physical closure remain immutable records of the result and interpretation observed before this route audit. R130 is an additive correction and supersedes that interpretation only for current and future authority."
  },
  "qualification_gap": {
